Modifications in this copy
--------------------------

CipherStash made these changes. The defect numbers are those of the audit
posted on cipherstash/skills#65.

- references/type-safety.md is adapted from skills/typescript-pro/
  references/type-guards.md, skills/typescript-pro/references/
  advanced-types.md, and the code examples and rules in
  skills/typescript-pro/SKILL.md. Its examples now live as TypeScript source
  in examples/src/type-safety/, with tests, and these changes are made:
  - the branded type from SKILL.md is reformatted by Biome and exported,
    and getOrder has an explicit return type and returns a lookup key
    instead of an empty body, so that it compiles under isolatedDeclarations
    and passes the lint suite;
  - the exhaustive switch from SKILL.md is reformatted by Biome and
    exported, its isSuccess guard is left out, and its error message passes
    the never value through JSON.stringify, which oxlint's
    restrict-template-expressions rule requires;
  - assertIsUser asserted a full User after checking only its type field;
    it checks every field (defect 15);
  - the satisfies example is new;
  - the rule to use an "Annotated pattern" with type predicates, a Python
    concept, is dropped (defect 1);
  - the variance examples marked "OK" were type errors, because string is
    not assignable to object; the rule is stated in prose with types for
    which it holds (defect 12);
  - the higher-kinded type example, which used any and never used its type
    parameter, is dropped (defect 13);
  - the redeclared NonNullable, Partial, Required, and intrinsic string
    types are dropped, and the reference says to use the standard library's
    types and never redeclare them (defect 14);
  - the rules say never to cast through any to satisfy a return type, as in
    "return null as any" (defect 20), and to type a field of unknown shape
    in a union as unknown, not any (defect 21);
  - the other type-guard and advanced-type examples are replaced by prose
    rules.
- references/error-handling.md is new. Upstream has no error handling
  reference.
- references/checks.md, the templates in assets/, examples/, and tests/
  are new.
- SKILL.md is new: a rule list and an index of references. Its type safety
  rules draw on the upstream SKILL.md constraints list. The upstream
  frontmatter metadata, persona line, workflow, output template, and
  related skills are not carried over. It targets TypeScript 7.0, not
  TypeScript 5.0 (defect 4), and drops tRPC from the description and
  triggers (defect 5).
- skills/typescript-pro/references/patterns.md and
  skills/typescript-pro/references/utility-types.md are not ported, so
  defects 16 to 19 in patterns.md leave with them.
- skills/typescript-pro/references/configuration.md is not ported here.
  The tsconfig.json template in assets/ replaces its compiler settings and
  the recommended tsconfig.json in the upstream SKILL.md.
